-Tagging workflows
    -DONE (v1): clicking a link opens the tag fields under the schedule in
     one popup — market path, GCA/LCA, source/sink, transmission
     reservations, carbon copy; the schedule comes from the link; Generate
     writes the workbook. Writes to TAG Bilateral WEST\Test while
     TEST_MODE is on.
    -DONE (v2): PSE codes come from BilateralMarketPseMapping, ranked by
     what our own tags use most, so nobody types the mapping; the sheet's
     two PSE cells are derived from the market path's ends.
    -DONE (v2): the OATI tag history (read-only) is assembled and grouped
     into route recipes — python scripts/export_tag_corpus.py --start
     2026-01-01 writes tag_corpus/ (gitignored).
    -DONE (v3): the transmission reservation number fills in its own path
     from our OASIS summary, and reports what it grants. Non-standard
     references (FCATBTEP and the like) are left alone.
    -TODO: parse the e-Tag path strings we exchange on ICE chat, using the
     corpus above as the ground truth. e.g.
     HE1-6; Mead MAG (G @ SWPW) (SWPP tx CRSP>PNPK, 2nh TBD)(WALC tx
     PPK>MEAD, 7f 110704717) - MAG - EEMU - TNSK - MGM sink. Needs the
     corpus of string-to-tag matches first. One schedule can split across
     paths, so a link can produce more than one tag — don't assume one.
    -DONE (v4): the link popup leads with the path string. It opens as
     ??-{buy PSE}-MAG001-{sell PSE}-??, sits in a copyable block above a
     paste box that takes each round back, and the tag fields moved behind
     an expander — shut on a link being drawn, open on one clicked again.
    -DONE (v5): "Lookup old tags", under the path string. Reads OATI
     history and ranks it against the link's own counterparties (always
     known, nothing typed) plus GCA/LCA once filled in — matching on the
     tag's structured fields, never the path string, which still can't be
     parsed. Every match is its own "Use this route" button, display-only
     until pressed: a choice, never a fill. Each is shown by where the
     power starts and ends, its PSE chain and its wheels — enough detail
     that no two cards read alike. A market end settles its control area,
     so a link into SWPW is never offered a CISO route, and its path
     string ends MAG001(s) rather than a placeholder. The popup runs the
     hours and the path string full width, puts the lookup beside the tag
     fields below them, and is packed so the whole tag fits on a 1080p
     screen without scrolling (1,988px -> 1,063). The market path and
     transmission editors are sized to their rows, so neither is ever
     scrolled and the popup grows with a longer route.
     Pressing one fills GCA/LCA, source/sink points and market path, and
     carries a reservation number only where it is still good for the flow
     date or isn't a dated reference at all — an expired one leaves the
     number blank and keeps its path.
    -DONE (v6): a link line now says two things without being clicked. It
     comes down into a market chip from above rather than in from the
     side, so several links reaching the rail no longer converge
     indistinguishably; and it is coloured by who still has to tag it —
     blue MAG, orange the counterparty, light grey done. The state is a
     radio in the popup's header for now: nothing on the board can infer
     it yet, and the colour repaints the board behind the open popup.
    -DONE (v6): a link sinking into SWPW opens with the desk's own
     convention already in its cells — SPP in the Market cell, SWPW as the
     LCA, the delivery point in the header (x-SWPW(CRSP)) and the Sink
     cell left empty, which "Use this route" then has to leave empty too.
     Every other market end still settles its own control area.
    -DONE (v6): the OASIS path fill no longer overrules a scheduler who
     empties the cell — a blank Path is filled once per reference, and a
     path of its own that goes stale still follows a changed number.
    -DONE (v6): what each market settles about the end of a link reaching
     it, as a table the desk can extend: the header piece, the Market cell
     and the control area for CAISO, AESO, SWPW and SWPP, none of which is
     the market's own name. CEN is left out until its own workbooks are
     handled.
    -DONE (v6): a quick-fill box per tag — one MW across every hour the
     link runs, since most tags carry the same number all day.
    -DONE (v6): found the data editor bug for real. `height` is hashed into
     a data editor's element id, so sizing an editor to its rows renamed it
     the moment a row went, and the deletion was looked up under a name
     that held nothing. Seed and identity now move together.
    -TODO: warn before Generate when a tag matches no route we have ever
     run — the cheapest typo-catcher available now the corpus exists.
    -DONE (v6): one link, several tags. The popup carries a tab per path
     the schedule is split down ("Split", up to six), each with its own
     hours, path string, lookup and fields; the link above them is
     unchanged. A check under the link's own total says so whenever the
     shares stop adding up to it, in either direction, and blocks Generate
     — which writes every tag of the link in one press. A new tag starts
     with no hours, so a split adds up the moment it is made.
    -TODO: tell the three kinds of tag apart, and let the popup say which
     one a link is. 1) MAG has to tag it. 2a) MAG doesn't, but its
     information is needed to. 2b) MAG doesn't and its information isn't
     needed — bilateral to bilateral, never into a market, and the whole
     job is carrying the string. Nothing in the app distinguishes them yet;
     the path string and the tag expander are shaped so that a 2b) link
     never has to open the expander.

